# The VabaxOS Start menu (vabaxos-start, block 12; ADR-0025, Vabax's
# choice C of 2026-09-26: for everyone, ArcMenu removed). Super and Super+S
# open it (vabaxos-keys); at the left of the taskbar the Start button with
# the VabaxOS logo and the word "Start" (an icon alone has no name for
# Orca), and a search box as in Windows 11 (vabaxos-keys, taskbarStart.js).
# The GNOME overview is on Super+Tab (30-windows-keys). Defaults: users can
# change them.
# All the extensions VabaxOS turns on (one list: blocks 3 and 8; the last
# one is VabaxOS's own, for the Windows keys and the Start button). Each
# one must pass vabaxos-a11y-check in test-boot.sh.
# button-names@vabaxos.org (vabaxos-accessibility, ADR-0022) names GNOME
# Shell's icon-only buttons, such as Close and Expand on notifications.
[org/gnome/shell]
enabled-extensions=['button-names@vabaxos.org', 'dash-to-panel@jderose9.github.com', 'ubuntu-appindicators@ubuntu.com', 'ding@rastersoft.com', 'GPaste@gnome-shell-extensions.gnome.org', 'tiling-assistant@leleat-on-github', 'vabaxos-keys@vabaxos.org']

# Dash to Panel without its "Show Applications" button: the Start button
# takes its place, as in Windows. Its own order of the other elements, for
# the first four screens (Dash to Panel reads them by screen number).
[org/gnome/shell/extensions/dash-to-panel]
